\label{lemma-local-isomorphism-implies}
Let $A \to B$ be a local isomorphism. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $A \to B$ is \'etale,
\item $A \to B$ identifies local rings,
\item $A \to B$ is quasi-finite.
\end{enumerate}
